        420
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 1,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "FLUX 3 Video → HDR Video\n\n1. Flux 3 Text to Video generates the clip through ComfyUI's API nodes (sign in to your Comfy account; the run uses API credits). Edit the prompt and settings there.\n2. Get Video Components splits the clip into frames, sound and frame rate.\n3. SDR → HDR Universal runs RUDRA ACES 2 (Auto, about 3 MB, downloaded on first run): a scene-linear master (1.0 = 203 nits) whose ACES 2.0 SDR view keeps the generated codes. reconstructed_mask marks where light was rebuilt; Video Frames keeps the clip in order.\n4. SDR → HDR AI Fill (RUDRA v3) is bypassed. Select it and press Ctrl+B to regenerate large blown highlights (needs Wan2.1-VACE-1.3B and a 16 GB GPU; downloaded on first use).\n5. The Viewer shows the master through ACES 2.0 against the SDR source: use the wipe to see what RUDRA rebuilt.\n6. Write saves a 16-bit half EXR sequence with a .wav at the first frame's timecode, and an HDR10 (PQ) MP4 with sound for review. Output: output/radiance_api/."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "FLUX 3 Video → HDR Video\n\n1. Flux 3 Text to Video generates the clip through ComfyUI's API nodes (sign in to your Comfy account; the run uses API credits). Edit the prompt and settings there.\n2. Get Video Components splits the clip into frames, sound and frame rate.\n3. SDR → HDR Universal runs RUDRA ACES 2 (Auto, about 3 MB, downloaded on first run): a scene-linear master (1.0 = 203 nits) whose ACES 2.0 SDR view keeps the generated codes. reconstructed_mask marks where light was rebuilt; Video Frames keeps the clip in order.\n4. SDR → HDR AI Fill (RUDRA v3) is bypassed. Select it and press Ctrl+B to regenerate large blown highlights (needs Wan2.1-VACE-1.3B and a 16 GB GPU; downloaded on first use).\n5. The Viewer shows the master through ACES 2.0 against the SDR source: use the wipe to see what RUDRA rebuilt.\n6. Write saves a 16-bit half EXR sequence with a .wav at the first frame's timecode, and an HDR10 (PQ) MP4 with sound for review. Output: output/radiance_api/."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
